WEBVTT

01:30.251 --> 01:33.001
Seventeen Poker  Fourth Hand

01:36.761 --> 01:42.261
<b>Counterattack</b>

01:37.141 --> 01:38.081
Huh?

01:38.081 --> 01:43.321
Kikuchi said knowing where the joker 
is would let him win for sure...

01:43.321 --> 01:44.891
Is it really that helpful?

01:45.181 --> 01:47.651
Akiyama got to cut second this hand,

01:47.651 --> 01:50.431
so the chances of them drawing 
the joker are even, right?

01:50.431 --> 01:51.551
That's right.

01:51.901 --> 01:55.961
And in fact, the joker isn't 
in Kikuchi's hand right now.

01:55.961 --> 01:56.951
Right?

01:57.161 --> 02:00.571
Even if the joker doesn't go
 to one of them to begin with,

02:00.571 --> 02:03.291
the chances of either one 
drawing it from the deck

02:03.291 --> 02:05.161
are still fifty-fifty.

02:05.161 --> 02:06.431
You're wrong.

02:07.521 --> 02:11.061
When Kikuchi gets to draw first,

02:11.061 --> 02:14.911
there's a 100% chance that 
Akiyama's not drawing the joker.

02:16.241 --> 02:19.921
Let's say the joker is
 on top of the deck.

02:20.111 --> 02:23.281
Kikuchi knows it's the joker,

02:23.281 --> 02:26.661
so if he draws first, 
he's guaranteed to get it.

02:27.411 --> 02:29.351
I understand that much, but...

02:29.721 --> 02:32.191
<i>You may now draw cards.</i>

02:32.361 --> 02:33.491
Kikuchi-san?

02:34.071 --> 02:37.441
I'll discard all five, then.

02:37.441 --> 02:39.641
His whole hand?! Why?!

02:39.641 --> 02:42.281
Because the joker is the fifth card down.

02:45.711 --> 02:47.001
You see now, don't you?

02:47.001 --> 02:49.851
If the joker is in the top five cards,

02:49.851 --> 02:52.871
Kikuchi will always be able to get it.

02:53.231 --> 02:59.361
But if it's the sixth or seventh 
card, won't Akiyama get it?

02:59.361 --> 03:00.871
Not likely.

03:00.871 --> 03:06.021
In Seventeen Poker, the worst hand 
you can start with is a pair.

03:06.021 --> 03:10.891
Which means Akiyama is unlikely 
to ask for more than three cards.

03:10.891 --> 03:12.371
I get it!

03:12.371 --> 03:14.991
Kikuchi can just ask for one or two.

03:14.991 --> 03:19.111
Then, since his opponent 
won't draw more than three,

03:19.111 --> 03:21.391
the last two cards go untouched!

03:21.391 --> 03:24.151
In other words, no matter where 
the joker is in the deck,

03:24.151 --> 03:26.541
Akiyama's never getting it.

03:26.791 --> 03:30.911
Kikuchi has overwhelmingly better 
odds of getting the joker.

03:31.251 --> 03:35.111
But isn't scrapping his 
whole hand kinda risky?

03:35.111 --> 03:36.741
Not at all.

03:36.741 --> 03:40.171
In the last draw, Akiyama took two cards.

03:40.171 --> 03:43.391
In other words, all seventeen 
cards have been used.

03:43.951 --> 03:45.071
Right...

03:45.071 --> 03:49.041
Of those seventeen, 
Kikuchi has seen ten of them.

03:49.041 --> 03:53.591
He can calculate back from that to figure
which seven his opponent has seen.

03:54.451 --> 03:57.131
No matter how you combine 
those seven cards,

03:57.131 --> 03:58.891
the best he could have is two pairs.

03:58.891 --> 04:01.201
Kikuchi's victory is a certainty.

04:01.691 --> 04:03.531
Open!

04:05.781 --> 04:07.781
<b>Eastern Army - Two Pair</b>

04:05.781 --> 04:07.781
<b>Western Army - Three of a Kind</b>

04:07.811 --> 04:08.841
Yes!

04:08.841 --> 04:11.281
<i>Kikuchi wins the fourth hand.</i>

04:11.291 --> 04:14.291
Chip Divide

04:11.291 --> 04:14.291
chip

04:11.291 --> 04:14.291
Eastern Army lead

04:11.501 --> 04:14.291
<i>Twenty chips go to the Western Army.</i>

04:16.661 --> 04:18.971
We will now begin the fifth hand.

04:25.591 --> 04:27.301
He got the joker!

04:27.301 --> 04:29.091
And four of a kind!

04:29.411 --> 04:31.901
Kikuchi-san, the first bet is yours.

04:33.451 --> 04:34.481
I fold.

04:36.161 --> 04:39.491
<i>The fifth hand is incomplete.</i>

04:39.481 --> 04:44.741
Chip Divide

04:39.481 --> 04:44.741
chip

04:39.481 --> 04:44.741
Eastern Army lead

04:39.491 --> 04:42.001
<i>Both five-chip antes go to the dealer.</i>

04:42.001 --> 04:44.741
<i>The chip balance does not change.</i>

04:45.761 --> 04:47.621
We had such a good hand, too...

04:47.861 --> 04:51.861
What do we do? Those precious 
chips went to the dealer...

04:52.131 --> 04:53.371
What happened there?

04:53.371 --> 04:55.871
His opponent drew the joker.

04:56.151 --> 04:59.411
If he folds, he basically forces a tie.

04:59.411 --> 05:03.251
And, having folded, he'll cut 
second in the next hand.

05:03.251 --> 05:06.921
He can arrange to nab the 
joker in his opening hand.

05:06.921 --> 05:08.371
I get it.

05:08.761 --> 05:10.641
Sixth Hand

05:14.141 --> 05:15.231
You see?

05:15.581 --> 05:16.991
Incredible.

05:16.991 --> 05:19.541
The first round of betting is complete.

05:19.541 --> 05:22.251
Now, open!

05:22.361 --> 05:24.481
<b>Western Army - Four of a Kind</b>

05:22.361 --> 05:24.481
<b>Eastern Army - Full House</b>

05:24.711 --> 05:25.611
Yes!

05:25.611 --> 05:27.991
<i>The Western Army wins 
the sixth hand, as well.</i>

05:27.991 --> 05:30.871
Chip Divide

05:27.991 --> 05:30.871
chip

05:27.991 --> 05:30.871
Eastern Army lead

05:28.271 --> 05:33.611
<i>Twenty chips go to the Western Army, 
who now takes the lead.</i>

05:30.871 --> 05:33.621
Chip Divide

05:30.871 --> 05:33.621
chip

05:30.871 --> 05:33.621
Western Army lead

05:39.121 --> 05:41.531
<i>The Core match is ours!</i>

05:41.921 --> 05:43.041
You...

05:43.991 --> 05:46.131
can see the joker, can't you?

05:46.131 --> 05:47.211
Wha...

05:47.211 --> 05:48.771
What are you talking about?

05:49.081 --> 05:51.741
You should've kept that under wraps.

05:51.741 --> 05:54.021
You're being way too obvious about it.

05:54.251 --> 05:56.511
Drawing four cards in the practice round

05:56.511 --> 05:59.021
and five in the fourth hand just now...

05:59.381 --> 06:02.771
Then folding when the joker 
was in my hand to start...

06:02.771 --> 06:06.171
There's only one way
 to explain your behavior.

06:06.171 --> 06:09.071
You know where the joker is.

06:09.651 --> 06:10.981
Impossible.

06:11.631 --> 06:15.611
They open a new pack each hand.

06:15.611 --> 06:17.501
There's no way to cheat.

06:17.741 --> 06:19.761
It's just your imagination.

06:20.061 --> 06:23.531
But of course, it's human nature 
to get jumpy when you're losing.

06:24.001 --> 06:25.251
I see.

06:25.251 --> 06:27.631
Maybe I am just getting jumpy.

06:27.831 --> 06:28.881
Time-out!

06:28.881 --> 06:31.221
<i>The Eastern Army calls their time-out.</i>

06:31.221 --> 06:34.521
<i>You will have three minutes to plan.</i>

06:34.521 --> 06:38.481
Looks like you're not the 
only one feeling jumpy.

06:42.001 --> 06:44.741
The Core match is as good as ours!

06:45.081 --> 06:46.111
He's caught on.

06:46.521 --> 06:50.151
He's realized I know where the joker is.

06:50.151 --> 06:51.371
Will you be all right?

06:51.371 --> 06:52.361
Oh, please.

06:52.361 --> 06:55.991
Even if he's caught on, 
there's nothing he can do about it.

06:56.261 --> 06:58.861
Only I can use this trick.

06:58.861 --> 07:00.401
Players of the Western Army!

07:02.131 --> 07:03.921
What's this all about?

07:04.231 --> 07:07.481
Please, can we call a truce?

07:10.421 --> 07:13.671
We want to save you!

07:13.671 --> 07:16.291
Where's this coming from?

07:16.291 --> 07:18.811
Hang on. Let's hear her out.

07:19.151 --> 07:23.401
We intentionally ended the 
Spearhead match in a tie.

07:23.401 --> 07:25.161
Do you understand why?

07:25.541 --> 07:29.301
To secure our victory, 
we would have had to pass,

07:29.301 --> 07:31.791
and a lot of chips would 
have gone to the dealer.

07:32.201 --> 07:36.711
In terms of the total pot, we, 
the players, would have lost out.

07:36.711 --> 07:39.141
What are you talking about? "Total pot"?

07:39.141 --> 07:42.641
In this revival round, 
they handed out 900 million in chips

07:42.641 --> 07:44.721
but are only collecting 600 million.

07:45.071 --> 07:48.551
We have a chance to nab 
that bonus 300 million.

07:48.961 --> 07:53.301
If we don't fight, that 300 million 
can save multiple people.

07:53.301 --> 07:56.061
If you'll agree to concede to us,

07:56.061 --> 07:59.991
we'll use it all to save the three of you!

08:00.411 --> 08:01.981
That's ridiculous.

08:01.981 --> 08:03.891
I think she means it.

08:03.891 --> 08:07.121
It's the only reason they'd go for 
a draw in the Spearhead match.

08:07.121 --> 08:08.431
Are you kidding?

08:08.431 --> 08:13.591
Nobody would shoot themselves 
in the foot to save someone else!

08:13.591 --> 08:14.951
Please!

08:15.351 --> 08:16.571
Drop it.

08:16.571 --> 08:19.461
They're not going to go for it.

08:20.431 --> 08:21.831
But...

08:21.831 --> 08:24.811
<i>Your time to strategize is up.</i>

08:24.811 --> 08:26.571
<i>Both players please...</i>

08:27.211 --> 08:29.091
Seventh Hand

08:33.781 --> 08:34.871
Hey.

08:35.631 --> 08:39.371
Is what that Kanzaki girl said true?

08:39.371 --> 08:41.811
About saving us?

08:41.811 --> 08:42.731
Yeah.

08:43.881 --> 08:46.711
That would certainly be nice.

08:47.681 --> 08:48.941
You hear that?

08:48.941 --> 08:51.701
He might accept our proposal!

08:52.641 --> 08:55.291
Now, your first bet, please.

08:55.291 --> 08:58.781
I bet the maximum: fifteen chips.

09:00.271 --> 09:02.891
What will you do, Akiyama-san?

09:02.891 --> 09:05.051
I'm sure you're going to call, right?

09:05.381 --> 09:10.161
Can't let the dealer take those chips 
if you really want to save us, right?

09:11.241 --> 09:12.451
I call.

09:13.861 --> 09:15.591
That's the way.

09:16.211 --> 09:19.161
I've got a bad feeling about this.

09:19.791 --> 09:22.081
Your second bet, please.

09:23.711 --> 09:26.991
The maximum thirty chips!

09:28.391 --> 09:29.701
Akiyama-san.

09:30.121 --> 09:32.731
You wanna save us, right?

09:33.921 --> 09:36.351
The five cards in my hand...

09:36.701 --> 09:40.511
They're absolute shit.
 You'll win this one for sure.

09:40.961 --> 09:44.121
No way you're dropping out now, right?

09:45.851 --> 09:46.861
Call.

09:46.861 --> 09:52.371
<i>Incredible. A big play 
for a full pot of fifty chips!</i>

09:52.371 --> 09:54.791
Now, open!

09:57.331 --> 10:01.651
<i>Kikuchi of the Western Army 
wins with four queens.</i>

10:04.551 --> 10:08.221
<i>Like I'd ever give myself a garbage hand!</i>

10:08.821 --> 10:12.741
<i>I knew the joker was 
the second card down.</i>

10:12.971 --> 10:15.911
<i>Since I always know where the joker is,</i>

10:15.911 --> 10:18.741
<i>I'm invincible in this game!</i>

10:18.741 --> 10:21.251
Nao! This is all your fault!

10:21.251 --> 10:24.811
Because <i>you</i> told him we can't 
let chips go to the dealer!

10:24.811 --> 10:28.251
So even when Akiyama can't win, 
he can't fold, either!

10:28.251 --> 10:30.281
N-No...

10:30.281 --> 10:33.491
<i>Another fifty chips to the Western Army.</i>

10:33.501 --> 10:40.261
Chip Divide

10:33.501 --> 10:40.261
chip

10:33.501 --> 10:40.261
Western Army lead

10:33.821 --> 10:36.561
<i>The divide is now 118 chips.</i>

10:36.561 --> 10:39.991
<i>With a mere three hands left 
to play, the gulf has grown wide.</i>

10:40.671 --> 10:44.751
I very kindly called 
on that fifty-chip bet,

10:44.751 --> 10:46.351
and you'd mock me for it?

10:47.091 --> 10:50.961
I suppose I'll really have to crush you.

10:52.571 --> 10:55.141
We will now begin the eighth hand.

10:55.571 --> 10:56.771
Wait a minute.

10:56.771 --> 10:58.821
You've been letting the cards show.

10:59.541 --> 11:02.061
Kikuchi's winning because 
he memorizes the cards

11:02.061 --> 11:04.151
he sees when you do the Hindu shuffle.

11:04.151 --> 11:08.111
What?! Don't make things up 
just because you're losing!

11:08.111 --> 11:09.651
I'm not making anything up.

11:10.211 --> 11:13.591
You clearly know where the joker is.

11:13.881 --> 11:15.541
Is he serious?!

11:15.841 --> 11:18.871
The LGT Office wants these 
games to be fair, correct?

11:18.871 --> 11:20.541
Well, yes...

11:20.891 --> 11:23.691
Why not stick to only 
the riffle shuffle, then?

11:24.241 --> 11:28.861
You won't be holding up the cards, 
so he won't be able to see them.

11:29.461 --> 11:33.831
If you want to prove your innocence, 
I'm sure you'll agree to that.

11:34.731 --> 11:36.091
Okay.

11:36.091 --> 11:38.201
I agree to just a riffle shuffle.

11:38.451 --> 11:40.571
If you please, then.

11:41.981 --> 11:43.561
<i>What an idiot!</i>

11:43.561 --> 11:47.071
<i>He can't stop my foolproof plan that way!</i>

11:47.351 --> 11:52.121
<i>The riffle shuffle is even easier 
to follow than the Hindu!</i>

11:53.781 --> 11:56.571
From here on out, 
it's every man for himself.

11:56.571 --> 11:58.541
I'll engage in these last
hands with cold logic...

11:58.981 --> 12:01.011
and destroy you.

12:01.441 --> 12:02.651
Is that right?

12:02.651 --> 12:04.521
<i>Boast all you want!</i>

12:04.521 --> 12:08.471
<i>No matter how you struggle, 
I'll still win the day!</i>

12:11.351 --> 12:13.791
<i>The joker is the fourth card down.</i>

12:14.481 --> 12:16.451
Your first bet, please.

12:16.921 --> 12:19.591
<i>If I want to make sure 
he stays in the game,</i>

12:19.591 --> 12:22.581
<i>I need him to think my hand is bad.</i>

12:22.581 --> 12:24.651
<i>Keep the bet small...</i>

12:24.651 --> 12:26.031
Five chips.

12:26.421 --> 12:28.311
Five? Huh.

12:28.871 --> 12:30.491
Akiyama-san, if you please.

12:32.681 --> 12:35.581
The maximum fifteen chips.

12:37.531 --> 12:38.681
Kikuchi-san?

12:39.891 --> 12:41.081
I call.

12:41.081 --> 12:45.351
<i>He stayed in the game because 
I kept my bet small!</i>

12:45.351 --> 12:47.741
You may now draw cards.

12:48.101 --> 12:50.841
<i>He won't take more than three.</i>

12:50.841 --> 12:54.031
<i>I'll get the joker no matter what.</i>

12:54.031 --> 12:55.971
I'll discard my whole hand.

12:55.971 --> 12:57.971
<i>What?!</i>

12:58.741 --> 13:01.851
<i>He's ended up with the joker!</i>

13:02.151 --> 13:04.801
Kikuchi-san, how many 
cards would you like?

13:05.271 --> 13:06.681
One, please.

13:10.131 --> 13:12.401
<i>This hand's better than I expected!</i>

13:13.091 --> 13:15.261
<i>The problem is Akiyama, though...</i>

13:15.261 --> 13:17.741
Akiyama-san, your second bet, please.

13:17.741 --> 13:19.951
<i>If he raises big, I'll fold.</i>

13:20.581 --> 13:22.761
I'll stick with fifteen.

13:22.761 --> 13:25.171
<i>He's not raising?</i>

13:25.171 --> 13:27.421
<i>Maybe his hand's not so great?</i>

13:27.421 --> 13:29.561
<i>I guess I got lucky!</i>

13:29.561 --> 13:31.381
Kikuchi-san, if you please.

13:33.211 --> 13:34.561
Call.

13:34.561 --> 13:36.561
Then... open!

13:38.381 --> 13:41.851
<i>The West has a full house. 
The East, four of a kind.</i>

13:43.781 --> 13:47.281
<i>The Eastern Army takes the eighth hand.</i>

13:47.281 --> 13:50.771
<i>The chip differential is now 48.</i>

13:47.281 --> 13:51.031
Chip Divide

13:47.281 --> 13:48.471
chip

13:47.281 --> 13:48.471
Western Army lead

13:48.471 --> 13:51.031
chip

13:48.471 --> 13:51.031
Western Army lead

13:51.041 --> 13:53.171
Akiyama-san is amazing!

13:53.491 --> 13:56.161
<i>It was inevitable that I'd 
lose like that eventually.</i>

13:56.461 --> 13:58.671
<i>Actually, it's to my benefit!</i>

13:58.671 --> 14:03.921
<i>Losing that hand gives 
me the second cut.</i>

14:04.131 --> 14:09.311
<i>Cutting second means I can get 
the joker in my opening hand!</i>

14:09.511 --> 14:12.471
<i>In other words, I'll win for sure!</i>

14:13.501 --> 14:15.761
We will now begin the ninth hand.

14:16.351 --> 14:18.721
Right. I'm turning it around now.

14:19.651 --> 14:21.321
<i>Whatever you say!</i>

14:21.631 --> 14:25.431
<i>I'll hang you with this hand.</i>

14:30.241 --> 14:31.621
I will now deal the cards.

14:31.621 --> 14:32.831
Wait a minute.

14:33.361 --> 14:37.141
Kikuchi peeked at the cards 
in that shuffle just now.

14:37.141 --> 14:39.081
Shuffle them again, please.

14:39.291 --> 14:40.991
More of your excuses?!

14:40.991 --> 14:42.941
What shall I do, Kikuchi-san?

14:43.831 --> 14:46.761
<i>I didn't expect him 
to harp on it like this,</i>

14:46.761 --> 14:50.781
<i>but it's better than refusing 
and looking like a cheater.</i>

14:51.131 --> 14:52.471
Go ahead.

14:54.181 --> 14:55.591
Will that do?

14:55.841 --> 14:57.431
That should be fine.

14:57.761 --> 15:00.211
The cut, then. Akiyama-san first.

15:00.621 --> 15:02.111
Five cards, then.

15:02.441 --> 15:03.861
Four cards.

15:03.861 --> 15:08.431
<i>That cut has moved the joker 
from the top to the fourth card.</i>

15:08.361 --> 15:13.511
Akiyama

15:08.361 --> 15:15.331
Kikuchi

15:09.111 --> 15:12.401
<i>The deal will start with Akiyama,</i>

15:12.401 --> 15:14.781
<i>and the joker will come to me!</i>

15:16.631 --> 15:19.991
<i>I already have three aces!</i>

15:19.991 --> 15:22.401
And now, the first round of betting.

15:23.801 --> 15:25.001
I'll check.

15:25.001 --> 15:26.661
<i>Check?!</i>

15:26.661 --> 15:30.811
<i>He wants to hold off and evaluate my hand?</i>

15:31.151 --> 15:32.951
<i>Let's keep it small.</i>

15:33.401 --> 15:34.581
Eight chips.

15:34.971 --> 15:37.911
Eight? Unexpectedly small.

15:38.601 --> 15:41.261
I'll call, then.

15:41.261 --> 15:43.491
<i>He's taken the bait!</i>

15:43.491 --> 15:46.111
Kikuchi-san, you may now draw.

15:46.471 --> 15:48.221
I'll take two cards.

15:50.271 --> 15:52.521
<i>A full house, aces high!</i>

15:52.521 --> 15:54.271
<i>Great insurance!</i>

15:54.271 --> 15:55.791
Akiyama-san?

15:57.461 --> 15:59.401
I'll take five, then.

15:59.401 --> 16:01.411
<i>Five cards?!</i>

16:02.161 --> 16:05.541
<i>What's with him? 
Is he just getting desperate?</i>

16:05.931 --> 16:08.551
The second round of betting 
will start with Kikuchi-san.

16:09.141 --> 16:14.041
<i>If I want to finish him off, 
I have to make sure he calls.</i>

16:14.381 --> 16:18.681
<i>To do that, I have to act 
like my hand is bad...</i>

16:18.681 --> 16:20.931
I'll bet... eight.

16:21.281 --> 16:22.591
Eight, hmm?

16:22.961 --> 16:24.821
And you, Akiyama-san?

16:24.821 --> 16:26.151
I'll raise.

16:26.151 --> 16:28.311
To the upper limit of thirty chips.

16:30.481 --> 16:32.751
<i>This guy's a bona fide moron!</i>

16:33.331 --> 16:37.031
<i>He thinks my hand is 
weak, so he's all in!</i>

16:37.031 --> 16:40.461
<i>I've never seen a bigger 
rube in all my life!</i>

16:40.461 --> 16:42.461
What will you do, Kikuchi-san?

16:43.231 --> 16:45.711
I suppose I'll have to call.

16:47.451 --> 16:49.211
<i>I can't stop smiling!</i>

16:49.451 --> 16:54.211
The hand is complete, with a 
whopping 43 chips on the line!

16:54.451 --> 16:55.221
Now...

16:55.521 --> 16:57.341
Open!

16:57.341 --> 16:59.841
<i>Die, Akiyama!</i>

17:01.471 --> 17:04.351
<b>Western Army - Full House</b>

17:01.471 --> 17:04.351
<b>Eastern Army - Four of a Kind</b>

17:05.641 --> 17:07.641
<i>Akiyama wins.</i>

17:07.641 --> 17:08.731
He did it!

17:08.731 --> 17:10.981
<i>The Eastern Army finally 
turns things around.</i>

17:11.751 --> 17:13.991
Chip Divide

17:11.751 --> 17:13.991
chip

17:11.751 --> 17:13.991
Eastern Army lead

17:13.091 --> 17:17.621
<i>The match will now be decided 
by the tenth and final hand.</i>

17:18.431 --> 17:21.241
<i>That was the dumbest of dumb luck.</i>

17:21.241 --> 17:26.371
<i>There's no way he'll draw four of 
a kind on a five-card draw again.</i>

17:26.601 --> 17:29.871
<i>And for the final hand, 
I get to cut second.</i>

17:29.871 --> 17:33.171
<i>I can guarantee the joker 
in my opening hand!</i>

17:33.791 --> 17:36.721
<i>Akiyama's losing for sure!</i>

17:38.181 --> 17:42.021
We will now begin the final hand.

17:42.021 --> 17:44.811
<i>I can win if the game plays out.</i>

17:44.811 --> 17:48.541
<i>But will he actually ride it out?</i>

17:48.541 --> 17:50.091
Don't worry.

17:51.051 --> 17:52.931
I'll stay in.

17:53.751 --> 17:57.631
You're worried I'll fold on the tenth hand

17:57.631 --> 18:01.711
to eke out a win in the Core match, right?

18:01.931 --> 18:04.971
Don't worry. I won't cut and run.

18:05.341 --> 18:08.201
The Spearhead match was a draw, remember?

18:08.201 --> 18:12.201
The important thing now 
isn't scrounging a win,

18:12.201 --> 18:15.941
but securing a large pot of chips so a 
loss in the General match won't stop us.

18:16.521 --> 18:18.871
Momentum is on my side at the moment,

18:18.871 --> 18:22.721
so if I think I can win, I'll definitely 
be looking to take a fifty-chip windfall.

18:23.101 --> 18:25.551
<i>Momentum's on his side, huh?</i>

18:26.781 --> 18:29.291
<i>Thank goodness he's so stupid!</i>

18:33.081 --> 18:35.821
<i>The joker is the ninth card down.</i>

18:35.821 --> 18:36.901
Wait.

18:36.901 --> 18:38.761
This is the final hand.

18:38.761 --> 18:41.771
Let's avoid any chance 
for doubt or resentment.

18:42.211 --> 18:44.011
Shuffle them three more times.

18:44.011 --> 18:45.191
This again?!

18:45.191 --> 18:46.551
I-I mean...

18:46.551 --> 18:49.911
Will that clear me in your mind?

18:50.141 --> 18:51.171
Yes.

18:51.721 --> 18:53.751
Then do it.

18:53.751 --> 18:55.071
As you wish.

19:02.521 --> 19:04.161
Now, the cut.

19:04.161 --> 19:05.301
Akiyama-san first.

19:05.621 --> 19:07.561
Eight cards, then.

19:07.561 --> 19:09.311
Seven cards.

19:09.311 --> 19:13.061
<i>The joker is sixth from the top.</i>

19:13.371 --> 19:16.651
<i>It'll come to me in my first hand!</i>

19:17.451 --> 19:19.661
<i>Aces-high full house!</i>

19:19.661 --> 19:22.821
<i>It's such a great hand, I can't 
stop myself from grinning!</i>

19:22.821 --> 19:23.661
<i>The question is...</i>

19:23.931 --> 19:27.371
<i>Will Akiyama stay in the game?</i>

19:27.371 --> 19:29.591
Now, the first round of betting.

19:31.421 --> 19:32.801
Fifteen chips.

19:34.031 --> 19:38.301
Didn't I tell you? 
I'm going all in if I think I can win.

19:38.611 --> 19:40.461
<i>I'm saved!</i>

19:40.461 --> 19:43.351
<i>His gambler's mindset is my salvation!</i>

19:43.351 --> 19:45.401
<i>He means to see this through to the end!</i>

19:46.001 --> 19:47.201
And you, Kikuchi-san?

19:47.201 --> 19:52.311
Well, since I'm behind and all, 
I suppose I'll just have to call.

19:52.311 --> 19:54.581
We'll now draw cards.

19:54.581 --> 19:55.761
Akiyama-san?

19:57.801 --> 19:59.941
I'll discard my whole hand.

20:02.371 --> 20:03.541
Is that a problem?

20:03.541 --> 20:05.641
Um, no...

20:06.331 --> 20:09.221
<i>He went all in with a trash hand?</i>

20:09.551 --> 20:15.711
<i>Or is he trading it out to increase 
his odds of getting the joker?</i>

20:15.961 --> 20:19.381
<i>Too bad it's already with me!</i>

20:19.721 --> 20:21.461
<i>Still, this is tricky...</i>

20:21.701 --> 20:26.001
<i>Since he drew five, if I draw two,</i>

20:26.001 --> 20:29.391
<i>we'll have gone through 
all seventeen cards.</i>

20:29.881 --> 20:35.791
<i>He'll realize I have the joker, 
and he'll drop out.</i>

20:36.141 --> 20:38.441
<i>I should stay strong, keep my hand,</i>

20:38.441 --> 20:44.361
<i>and act like the joker is one 
of the cards still in the deck.</i>

20:44.911 --> 20:46.871
All five cards, huh?

20:47.191 --> 20:51.201
Maybe my lousy hand 
stands a chance after all.

20:52.211 --> 20:54.631
Okay, I'll keep my hand.

20:54.631 --> 20:58.341
It's possible I could improve
my hand by drawing,

20:58.341 --> 21:02.121
but then you might fold, so...

21:02.451 --> 21:05.621
I'll face you down with 
this mediocre hand!

21:06.521 --> 21:08.311
<i>Did my performance convince him?</i>

21:08.811 --> 21:11.381
<i>Or was it too obvious?!</i>

21:11.761 --> 21:14.041
Now, the second round of betting.

21:14.041 --> 21:15.771
Akiyama-san, if you please.

21:15.771 --> 21:18.641
<i>I'm begging you, stay in!</i>

21:20.841 --> 21:22.021
Then...

21:22.551 --> 21:24.791
I'm in with thirty chips.

21:26.811 --> 21:28.811
What did you just say?

21:29.761 --> 21:33.641
I said I'm putting in the 
maximum bet. Thirty chips.

21:34.121 --> 21:35.631
Really?

21:36.001 --> 21:40.031
<i>I won... with the power of my acting!</i>

21:40.381 --> 21:42.601
Kikuchi-san, what will you do?

21:42.961 --> 21:45.631
I have no choice. I'll have to call.

21:45.631 --> 21:48.111
Then the hand is complete.

21:52.841 --> 21:55.391
You're an idiot, Akiyama!

21:56.291 --> 22:00.151
Now that the hand is complete, 
I'll tell you everything!

22:00.331 --> 22:02.691
You were right all along!

22:02.691 --> 22:05.541
I knew exactly where the joker was!

22:05.941 --> 22:09.311
This hand is mine!

23:45.081 --> 23:50.081
Next Time

23:45.081 --> 23:50.081
<b>General Match</b>
